# Tool-call streaming (local fix, opt-in): TF_GLM_STREAM_CALLS=1 sends a GLM call's header and argument fragments as they are written, instead of holding each call whole until its </tool_call> (patches 0053/0055). An agent client then sees a large write/edit call arrive continuously rather than in one delta after tens of seconds of silence. A call cut by the token limit is then sent only in part; finish_reason "length" marks it. Default 0 is the recipe's whole-call behavior.

